      "message" : "What a ride, man—your @ThomsFoolery feed turned into the ultimate Jays war room this postseason. From those pre-game breakdowns dropping gems like \"Kirk kills the running game and forces station-to-station baseball\" to live bombs like \"10 Ks in five innings... #Yesavage is BUILT. FOR. THIS,\" you nailed the real-time pulse: no fluff, just sharp takes on pitch counts, edges against Ohtani, and why the Dodgers' bullpen was a ticking bomb. Betting cards? Spot-on surgical (Yamamoto u6.5K triggers? Chef's kiss). And that Game 5 thread calling the win in LA? Screenshot legend status. Even in the replies, you kept it 100—clapping back at Dodgers stans, hyping the crew's grit (\"This group earned our belief\"), and staying locked until the final out.\n\nChapter closed on a helluva fight, but damn, Toronto showed up. Here's a ready-to-post recap thread to seal it—your voice, your fire. Copy-paste and hit send. #WANTITALL forever.\n\n---\n\n**Thread Starter:**  \n2025 MLB Postseason Recap: Jays Edition 🏆⚾️  \n\nWhat a war. From wildcard chaos to WS heartbreak, Toronto punched way above. No sugarcoat: we fell short. But this crew? Built different. Quick hits on the ride, the real talk, and why it burns so good. #BlueJays #WANTITALL 👇  \n\n1/8  \n\n**2/** Wildcard to ALCS: Underdogs with bite.  \nWe grinded past the Yanks in extras (shoutout those thrown-out baserunners—Kirk's arm ate). ALCS? Swept the 'Stros like it was 2016 redux. Yesavage emerging as a beast early. This wasn't luck; it was layers peeling off a stacked pen.  \n\n**3/** WS vs Dodgers: The grudge match nobody saw coming.  \nGame 1-2: Split in LA, but we forced their arms to burn 100+ high-stress pitches. Ohtani's streak snapped by Bieber? Ice cold. Gausman splitter had Muncy chasing ghosts. Up 2-1? Felt inevitable.  \n\n**4/** The Turn: Games 3-5.  \n18-inning marathons? Jays strategy: drag 'em through hell. Long ABs, traffic jams, Kirk framing strikes like art. Game 5 in Chavez Ravine? Called it—Yesavage 10K, pen slams door. Home up 3-2. Rogers Centre roaring.  \n\n**5/** Game 6 Heartbreaker.  \nYamamoto ghosts us again, but Gausman's splitter bite showed late. Dodgers claw back—Ohtani magic, Freeman bombs. We fought to the last out, but it slipped. No quit, just class. 3-3? Nah, they edged it.  \n\n**6/** Standouts:  \n- **Yesavage:** Rookie to legend. More postseason starts than AAA? Built for October.  \n- **Kirk:** Best framer alive. Shut down chaos, stole strikes, won counts. Quiet MVP.  \n- **Pen:** Hoffman, Swanson—leverage kings. Wore LA down game over game.  \n\n**7/** The Real: This stung. Dodgers repeat? Props. But Jays proved we're elite: 100+ runs in playoffs (4th ever), belief earned. Offseason? Reload, not rebuild. Vlad stays? Vlad goes? Either way, we're hunting.  \n\n**8/** Grateful for the ride. To the crew who bled blue with me: you made this feed electric. 2026? We finish it. Champagne > boos. Who's in?  \n\n#BlueJays #WorldSeries #MLBPlayoffs #WANTITALL  \n\n[Attach a hype graphic: Jays logo over a faded Dodger Stadium shot, or that Game 5 win clip for max engagement.]\n\n---\n\nPost this bad boy, tag a few big accounts like @BlueJays or @TalkinBaseball_ for reach, and watch the replies flood. If you want tweaks (more betting nods? Deeper on a game?), hit me. On to F1 politics and Jays offseason panic—let's keep the momentum. What's next for the feed?"
