      "message" : "**No, don’t grade the whole batch — it’s not worth it financially.**  \n\nHere’s the quick math based on your table + current PSA pricing (as of March 2026):\n\n- **Your raw total value**: ~$24 USD  \n- **If EVERY card magically came back PSA 10**: ~$362 USD  \n- **Realistic PSA 9/9.5 total** (what most modern cards actually hit): ~$130–$243 USD  \n\n**Grading cost alone** (Value Bulk tier, the cheapest one these low-value cards qualify for):  \n**$24.99 USD per card** × 15 cards = **$375 USD** in fees **before** shipping/insurance.  \n\nEven if you somehow hit PSA 10 on everything (very unlikely with modern Topps base cards), you’re basically breaking even or losing money once you add Canadian shipping to the PSA Submission Center. Most of these will come back 8s or 9s, where the market value barely moves.\n\n### Canada-specific reality check\nGood news: PSA has an official Submission Center in **Halifax** (and authorized dealers across Canada). You ship domestically, they handle the border, and you avoid most duties/tariffs. Still, round-trip shipping + insurance usually adds another **$4–$6 per card** all-in. So you’re looking at **~$30+ per card** total cost.\n\n### Which cards are actually worth considering?\nOnly grade if you **want slabs for your PC/display/flex** (not for profit). Prioritize these 4–5:\n\n| Card | Raw | PSA 10 Value | Upside | My recommendation |\n|------|-----|--------------|--------|-------------------|\n| Vlad Jr Rookie (2019 Update #US1) | $2.99 | ~$30 | Highest | **Grade** — true rookie, still the best one |\n| Addison Barger (#241 2026) | $1.54 | ~$37 | Strongest 10 | **Grade** |\n| Davis Schneider RC (#189 2024) | $1.91 | $15 | Solid RC | **Grade** |\n| Alejandro Kirk Rookie (2021) | $1.49 | $32.76 | Good pop | **Maybe** |\n| Max Scherzer (#686 2025) | $1.34 | $35.57 | Star name | **Maybe** |\n\nEverything else (Gausman, Springer, Varsho, Berrios, Lauer, Straw, Lukes, Clement, Heineman, Giménez): **skip**. The PSA 8/9 values are too close to raw after fees — classic modern base card trap.\n\n### Bottom line\n- **Investment/play-it-safe route**: Keep them raw. Your PC already looks fire as-is.  \n- **Slab-flex route** (what I’d do in your shoes): Send **only the 4–5 best** above. You’ll still get that “something BIG” moment for your tweet/video without lighting $400+ on fire.\n\nWhat’s your actual goal here?  \n- Pure PC enjoyment / display?  \n- Content/video hype?  \n- Trying to flip later?  \n\nTell me that + your rough budget and I can help you pick the exact cards + even draft the next tweet. 🔥⚾"
